Study area
The study area is Poltava oblast (COD-AB P-code UA53, English name in COD-AB “Poltavska”). It suits a reference test because it has:

towns (Poltava, Kremenchuk, Lubny and others), where soil maps have no data;
the Dnipro river and the Kremenchuk reservoir, where soil maps have no data and the DEM is flat;
seven neighbouring oblasts, so that some parcels cross an oblast boundary;
a band north of 50°N where the Copernicus DEM tiles have a coarser longitude spacing.




Reference parcels (centroids), elevators and roads in Poltava oblast. Details on the Reference inputs page.

Method, 2019–2024
06-crop.R has one explicit block per year, with the year written out in full. For each year:

rast(crop_2019) is read and NAflag(r) &lt;- 0 is set: code 0 is NoData (background) in every year;
the parcels are transformed to the map’s CRS (EPSG:32636); the 10 m map is never reprojected;
exact_extract(r, p, "frac") gives, for each parcel, the share of its classified area in each code. Each 10 m pixel is weighted by the share of it inside the parcel, and NoData pixels are left out of the total;
the codes are joined to crop_groups; codes not in the table become "other";
shares are summed by group, and missing groups are completed with 0, so every parcel has all 7 groups.

A parcel entirely on NoData would get 0 for every group; the script prints how many there are each year.

Script: 06-crop.R

# 06-crop.R
# In:  data/clean/reference/parcels.parquet, crop maps crop_2019 ... crop_2024, crop_groups (from 00-setup.R)
# Out: data/interim/long_crop.parquet
# Purpose: share of each parcel in 7 crop groups, one explicit block per year 2019-2024.

source("00-setup.R")

parcels &lt;- arrow::read_parquet(parcels_path, as_data_frame = FALSE) |&gt; st_as_sf()

# "frac" is the share of the parcel's classified (non-NoData) area in each code.
# 0 is NoData in every year. A parcel entirely on NoData gets 0 for all groups;
# the number of such parcels is printed for each year.

# 2019 ------------------------------------------------------------------------

r &lt;- rast(crop_2019)
NAflag(r) &lt;- 0
p &lt;- st_transform(parcels, crs(r))

crop_long_2019 &lt;- exact_extract(r, p, "frac", append_cols = "parcel_id", progress = FALSE) |&gt;
  pivot_longer(starts_with("frac_"), names_to = "code", names_prefix = "frac_",
               names_transform = as.integer, values_to = "share", values_drop_na = TRUE) |&gt;
  left_join(crop_groups, by = "code") |&gt;
  mutate(group = coalesce(group, "other")) |&gt;
  summarise(value = sum(share), .by = c(parcel_id, group)) |&gt;
  complete(parcel_id = parcels$parcel_id,
           group = c("built", "ag", "forest", "grass", "bare", "water", "other"),
           fill = list(value = 0)) |&gt;
  mutate(variable = str_c("crop_", group, "_2019"))

n_empty_2019 &lt;- crop_long_2019 |&gt; summarise(total = sum(value), .by = parcel_id) |&gt; filter(total == 0) |&gt; nrow()
cli_inform("2019: {n_empty_2019} parcel{?s} entirely on NoData.")

